        "A morpheme is the smallest unit of language that carries meaning or grammatical function. Free morphemes stand alone as words, like book, run and happy, while bound morphemes attach to others, like the plural s, the past ed and prefixes such as un. The word cats contains two morphemes, cat plus plural s, and unhappiness contains three. Counting morphemes rather than letters or syllables is the first skill of {S} morphology.",
