        "Choose the subscription correctly. Dear Sir must close with Yours faithfully, because the addressee is unnamed; Dear Mrs Bello must close with Yours sincerely. Mixing them, as in Dear Sir with Yours sincerely, is the classic layout fault. Examiners in {S} papers deliberately set both salutations in one question to catch guesswork.",
